@page 53 morning-prayer
c __MORNING PRAYER.__
Q ¶ __Or this Canticle:__
T __Benedicite, omnia Opera Domini.__
I O All ye Works of the Lord, bless ye the
  Lord: praise him, and magnify him for
  ever.
P O ye Angels of the Lord, bless ye the Lord:
  praise him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Heavens, bless ye the Lord: praise
  him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Waters that be above the firmament,
  bless ye the Lord: praise him, and magnify him
  for ever.
P O all ye Powers of the Lord, bless ye the
  Lord: praise him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Sun and Moon, bless ye the Lord:
  praise him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Stars of heaven, bless ye the Lord:
  praise him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Showers and Dew, bless ye the Lord:
  praise him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Winds of God, bless ye the Lord: praise
  him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Fire and Heat, bless ye the Lord: praise
  him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Winter and Summer, bless ye the Lord:
  praise him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Dews and Frosts, bless ye the Lord:
  praise him, and magnify him for ever.
P O ye Frost and Cold, bless ye the Lord:
f praise
